// posteditWideChangeFiles is where CALLERS and SIGNATURE RISK stop being help and start
// being noise. Measured on REP50's 49 gated pairs, bucketed by how many files the NO-TOOL
// arm's patch touched (a pre-treatment property, so this is not division bias):
//
//   1 file    n=26, 33.7% of baseline tokens, pooled  -0.91%
//   2-3 files n=14, 38.2% of baseline tokens, pooled +19.36%
//   4+ files  n= 9, 28.1% of baseline tokens, pooled -20.40%
//
// The 4+ bucket alone costs the pooled result 5.73 points. The mechanism is not retrieval —
// the payload named the edited file in 84.8% of sessions and the misses did no worse — it is
// that losing sessions do MORE work after the first edit (corr(delta post-edit shell, saving)
// = -0.747; losers +6 shell calls and +1 edit, to the SAME files). A change already spanning
// several files multiplies the callers/risk payload without narrowing what is left to do, so
// past this width the sections are withheld and only CHANGED plus VERIFY are emitted.
// Suppression is REPORTED, never silent: the counts survive so a reader knows what was held.
posteditWideChangeFiles = 4

